---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  current="ecosystem"
  title="StackPilot ecosystem — gODtECH"
  description="How StackPilot, gODtECH FORGE and gODtECH Steward work together without becoming one coupled system."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> gODtECH ecosystem</div>
      <h1><span class="gradient-text">Build it.</span><br />Keep it healthy. Govern the work.</h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">StackPilot, FORGE and Steward solve different problems on purpose. Their value increases when the boundaries stay clear.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:34px">
        <img src="/StackPilot/stackpilot-hero.svg" alt="StackPilot production-minded scaffolding header" style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:20px" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-kicker">Product boundaries</div>
        <h2>Three tools. Three jobs.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card"><span class="card-label">01 / FORGE</span><h3>Orchestrate</h3><p>Prepare bounded context, classify risk, govern approvals, coordinate workflows and collect evidence around AI-assisted engineering.</p><a class="button" href="https://github.com/gODtECH-Ctl-Create/gODtECH-FORGE" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore FORGE ↗</a></div>
        <div class="card"><span class="card-label">02 / STACKPILOT</span><h3>Scaffold</h3><p>Choose golden paths, render recipes, validate generated project structure and keep stack-aware readiness in one dedicated system.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/StackPilot/">StackPilot home</a></div>
        <div class="card"><span class="card-label">03 / STEWARD</span><h3>Maintain</h3><p>Scan repositories deterministically, report health findings and apply only explicit, conservative maintenance fixes.</p><a class="button" href="https://github.com/gODtECH-Ctl-Create/gODtECH-Steward" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore Steward ↗</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-kicker">Integration</div>
        <h2>Connect through contracts, not copied implementations.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">StackPilot can observe a versioned Steward scan. FORGE can orchestrate both tools when a workflow needs scaffolding and repository-health evidence. Each product remains independently usable.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;line-height:1.9">
        <div>FORGE <span style="color:var(--muted)">→ orchestrate / govern / verify</span></div>
        <div>&nbsp;&nbsp;├── StackPilot <span style="color:var(--muted)">→ scaffold / golden paths / readiness</span></div>
        <div>&nbsp;&nbsp;└── Steward <span style="color:var(--muted)">→ housekeeping / health / evidence</span></div>
        <div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;↓</div>
        <div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;TARGET PROJECT</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="callout">
        <div><h2>Use the smallest tool that solves the problem.</h2><p>Start with StackPilot for foundations, Steward for repository health, and FORGE for governed cross-tool engineering workflows.</p></div>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/StackPilot/">Back to StackPilot →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
